meta {
  name: Submit KYC
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/kyc
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "accountId": "{{senderAccountId}}",
    "fullName": "Jane Doe",
    "documentId": "PASSPORT-123456",
    "documentType": "PASSPORT",
    "attachments": [
      { "label": "passport-photo", "reference": "s3://bucket/passport.jpg" }
    ],
    "notes": "Submitted via Bruno for manual testing"
  }
}

docs {
  POST /kyc — closes the gap CLAUDE.md used to document ("no HTTP submit/
  verify endpoint"): a KycProfile could previously only be marked VERIFIED
  by saving one directly through KycProfileRepository (tests or an ad-hoc
  script).

  Mocked verification: this MVP auto-verifies every submission
  synchronously (status is VERIFIED immediately in the response) instead of
  calling a real KYC provider — same spirit as MockExchangeRateProvider /
  InMemoryComplianceChecker elsewhere in this codebase.

  Two things get written on success:
    1. A KycProfile row in Postgres (VERIFIED) — this is what
       ComplianceChecker actually reads when SendRemittanceUseCase checks
       whether the sender can move an amount above the unverified threshold.
    2. A "dossier" document in MongoDB (kyc_dossiers collection) — the raw
       submitted material (documentType, attachments, notes) — non-fatal:
       if Mongo is unreachable, the KycProfile above still gets saved and
       this request still succeeds, just without archiving the dossier that
       time.

  accountId/fullName/documentId are required — attachments/documentType/
  notes are optional. Resubmitting for the same accountId reuses the same
  kycProfileId/createdAt rather than creating a second profile (one profile
  per account, matching the schema's UNIQUE(account_id) constraint).

  Prerequisites (run in order):
    1. Account / Create Account (Sender)
    2. Auth / Login

  After running this, Remittance / Send Remittance can move amounts above
  the 100000 minor-unit unverified-sender threshold without a 403
  (ComplianceRejectedError).
}
